  "provenance_note": "Hand-derived from 732.0-B-5 EC1 §4.1.2 (Primary Header: version 01, SCID bits 2-9 and 42-43, VCID bits 10-15, VC Frame Count bits 16-39, Replay Flag bit 40, VC Frame Count Usage Flag bit 41, Cycle bits 44-47), §4.1.4 (the Transfer Frame Data Field), §4.1.6 (FECF), and §4.3.5.4 and §4.3.6.3 (a frame of a VCID or SCID that is not valid is discarded by the receiving end). The inputs are those of the cases they replace (aos-inv-dec-007 and -008, aos-oid-dec-002, aos-scid-dec-004, marked superseded by RS-023 / issue #232). A decode of a frame of a channel the configuration does not hold reads it as opaque octets: no M_PDU or B_PDU Header, no OCF, no Security Header or Trailer; `AosFrame::validate` rejects it with UnknownChannel (docs/standards/aos-frame.md, Order of the decoder's checks). Expected values read off the octets by the field widths above. The independent model of the other vector files of this codec (TV-023) does not cover this file: it was written before the change and is not touched by it; a blind-model round is the maintainer's decision (issue #232). Author: an AI agent, Claude Sonnet 5.5.",
